@startuml creation-flow
title TripTailor - Itinerary Creation Flow

actor User
participant Frontend
participant "Backend API\n(Spring Boot)" as API
participant "GenAI Service\n(Python)" as AI
participant "Travel Context\n(Python)" as Context
database "PostgreSQL\n(owned by Backend)" as DB
cloud "Geocoder\nNominatim / Photon" as Geo
cloud "Events / Weather\nSerpApi / Open-Meteo" as Providers
cloud "Configured LLM" as LLM

User -> Frontend : Enter trip details
Frontend -> API : POST /trips
API -> AI : POST /schedules
AI -> Context : POST /trip-context
Context -> Context : Check per-replica TTL caches
Context -> Geo : Geocode destination
note right of Geo
  Nominatim is primary.
  Photon is the fallback.
end note
Geo --> Context : Coordinates + country metadata
Context -> Providers : Fetch optional events + weather
Providers --> Context : Provider responses
Context --> AI : Best-effort trip context
note right of AI
  If travel context fails, generation
  continues without enrichment.
end note
AI -> LLM : OpenAI-compatible structured request
LLM --> AI : Schedule JSON
AI -> AI : Validate schema, exact dates,\n3-5 activities/day and unique blocks
AI --> API : Return validated schedule
API -> DB : Insert trip, days, activities
DB --> API : Saved trip
API --> Frontend : Return itinerary

@enduml
